<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Dec consumer prices up 0.2 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Dec consumer prices up 0.2 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo area consumer prices rose 0.2 percent in December from a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices increased 0.5 percent in November, the Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>For calendar 1996, Tokyo area consumer prices were unchanged from the previous year.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>				 DEC	  NOV	  OCT</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index     99.9	 99.8	 100.1</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	 +0.2 pct   +0.1 pct     0.0 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes     +0.1 pct   -0.3 pct    +0.1 pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index	 100.0	100.1	 100.1</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	 -0.1 pct   -0.1 pct    -0.1 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes     -0.1 pct    0.0 pct    +0.1 pct</p>
<p>				1996	 1995</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index    100.0	100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  0.0 pct   -0.3 pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index	 100.0	100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  0.0 pct   -0.1 pct</p>
<p>				   Nov	  Oct	 Sept</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index 100.3	100.6	100.4</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	   +0.5 pct   +0.5 pct    0.0 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	 -0.3 pct   +0.2 pct   +0.4 pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index    100.6	100.5	100.4</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	   +0.4 pct   +0.2 pct   +0.2 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	 +0.1 pct   +0.1 pct   +0.5 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: The Tokyo index was calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. The core index, which is a key barometer for gauging core inflation, is overall prices minus fresh food prices. The base year was changed to 1995 from 1990.)</p>
</text>
